.TH "Holberton " "SIMPLE SHELL" 2026-08-30 GNU
.SH NAME
Holberton Simple Shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple command ine interpreter that reads and executes commands from standard input. it displays the prompt 
.B #cisfu$
and waits for the user to type a command, after that it reads commands piped through standard input without displaying the prompt.
.SH COMMAND EXECUTION
When a command is entered, 
.B hsh
reads the line using 
.B getline 
and tokenizes it using spaces, tabs, and newlines as delimiters. 
If the command begins with a slash (/) or a dot (.), it treats the command as an absolute or relative path. If not, it searches the directories listed in the
.B PATH
environment variable to find the executable. It then uses the 
.B fork
and 
.B execve
system calls to execute the command in a child process, suspending the parent process until the child terminates.
.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
The following builtin commands are handled directly by the shell:
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell immediately.
.TP
.B env
Prints all current environment variables to standard output.
